cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "riemann-zeta-experiments: computational research on Riemann zeta zeros, pair correlation, Fourier optimization, and adjoint methods"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - alias: minamocake
repository-code: "https://github.com/minamocake/riemann-zeta-experiments"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  Research code for bounding multiplicities of zeta zeros with Montgomery's pair-correlation
  method. Includes exact rational certificates, a result registry that separates computational
  verification from the status of mathematical assumptions, the preserved pre-audit prototype,
  and an independent audit. All results assume the Riemann Hypothesis; no new theorem is claimed.
keywords:
  - Riemann zeta function
  - pair correlation
  - simple zeros
  - Fourier optimization
  - exact certificates
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Pair correlation estimates for the zeros of the zeta function via semidefinite programming"
    authors:
